Package: amatrix
Type: Package
Title: Backend-Agnostic Matrix Extensions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Bradley", "Buchsbaum", email = "brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Dense and sparse matrix classes that extend the 'Matrix'
    package and dispatch linear-algebra operations to interchangeable
    computational backends. A reference CPU backend is included; optional GPU
    backends ('MLX', 'OpenCL', 'Metal', 'ArrayFire') are provided by separate
    packages and are used only when installed, with automatic fallback to the
    CPU. Also provides cached Cholesky, QR and singular value
    factorizations, least-squares and ridge regression fitters, and
    randomized and block Krylov methods for truncated singular value
    decompositions.
URL: https://bbuchsbaum.github.io/amatrix/, https://github.com/bbuchsbaum/amatrix
BugReports: https://github.com/bbuchsbaum/amatrix/issues
